# Normalize line endings on checkout for every platform.
#
# GitHub's Windows runner checks out with git's default `core.autocrlf=true`,
# which rewrites every text file to CRLF. Prettier's default `endOfLine: "lf"`
# then reports the whole tree as unformatted, so `npm run format:check` failed
# on windows-latest only — every file flagged, with no real formatting issue.
#
# `text=auto` lets git detect text vs binary; `eol=lf` pins the working-tree
# ending to LF regardless of the platform default. Every tracked file in this
# repo is already LF, so this changes no content — it only stops Windows from
# converting on checkout.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary artifacts git should never touch.
*.node binary
*.png binary
*.icns binary
*.ico binary
*.sqlite3 binary
